Third-party material
--------------------

Construct Classic, Copyright (C) 2007-2012 Scirra Ltd., released as free software:
the editor under the GNU GPL version 2 or later, the runtime under a BSD-style licence.
Source: https://sourceforge.net/projects/construct/ (mirror: https://github.com/aolko/construct)

ccdec contains material derived from the Construct Classic editor source code:
  * ccdec/cap_tokens.py   - a port of the editor's expression tokenizer
                            (IDE/Editors/Expressions/CExpression.cpp)
  * ccdec/data/aces.json  - condition/action/expression descriptions extracted from the
                            editor and plugin sources by tools/gen_aces.py
  * the .cap and .exe data layouts implemented in ccdec/cap_format.py and ccdec/reader.py
    follow the editor's and runtime's serialization code.

tests/samples/mesh_editor/ ("Mesh Editor.cap" and "Mesh Editor.exe") is the Mesh Editor
tool shipped in the Construct Classic source tree (IDE/Tools/Mesh Editor), used as a test
reference under the same licence.

